        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "a9a6b228-2b59-5822-81a8-96575f88892e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: John Charles Cutler, John F. Mahoney\n- Organizations: United States Public Health Service, Venereal Disease Research Laboratory\n- Events: Tuskegee syphilis experiment, Terre Haute prison experiments\n- Concepts: syphilis, sexually transmitted diseases\n\nFacts:\n- John Charles Cutler was born on June 29, 1915, and he later became a senior surgeon and acting chief of the venereal disease program in the United States Public Health Service.\n- The Tuskegee Study of Untreated Syphilis in the Negro Male was conducted by the U.S. Public Health Service from 1932 to 1972.\n- The Tuskegee syphilis experiment observed the natural progression of untreated syphilis in rural African-American men in Alabama while presenting the study as free health care from the United States government.\n- The Terre Haute prison experiments were conducted in 1943 and 1944 by Dr. John C. Cutler under Dr. John F. Mahoney.\n- John F. Mahoney headed the Venereal Disease Research Laboratory of the U.S. Public Health Service during the Terre Haute prison experiments.\n- The Terre Haute prison experiments sought to determine the effectiveness of treatments for sexually transmitted diseases.\n- John Charles Cutler died on February 8, 2003.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "1360e922-5081-53da-b75a-a874ef64f99d",
        "text": "Page: John Charles Cutler. Sentence: John Charles Cutler (June 29, 1915 – February 8, 2003) was a senior surgeon, and the acting chief of the venereal disease program in the United States Public Health Service.\nPage: Tuskegee syphilis experiment. Sentence: The Tuskegee Study of Untreated Syphilis in the Negro Male, also known as the Tuskegee Syphilis Study or Tuskegee Syphilis Experiment ( ) was an infamous clinical study conducted between 1932 and 1972 by the U.S. Public Health Service.\nPage: Tuskegee syphilis experiment. Sentence: The purpose of this study was to observe the natural progression of untreated syphilis in rural African-American men in Alabama under the guise of receiving free health care from the United States government.\nPage: Terre Haute prison experiments. Sentence: The Terre Haute prison experiments were conducted by Dr. John C. Cutler in 1943 and 1944 under Dr. John F. Mahoney, the head of the Venereal Disease Research Laboratory of the US Public Health Service, to determine the effectiveness of treatments for sexually transmitted diseases.",
